cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "regressselect: regression test selection with measured safety loss"
abstract: >-
  Three regression test selection strategies scored on the same held-out
  revisions: import-graph reachability as the dependency-based baseline,
  smoothed historical co-failure prioritisation measured with APFD, and a
  gradient-boosted selector over change features producing a ranked order with
  a per-test probability. All three are evaluated by seeded fault injection into
  a bundled sample project on faults detected against tests run with the
  full-suite upper bound shown, and on safety loss, the fraction of real
  failures a selection would have missed. On the bundled fixtures the
  dependency baseline wins on both metrics and that result is reported
  unchanged. Research-grade; not flight-qualified, not certified, not approved
  for operational aerospace use.
